Verified byte-identical to the published copies on 2026-08-19, fetched from
https://ekr.financnasprava.sk/Formulare/XSD/<filename>

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The KV schemas stamp a VINTAGE, not a REVISION. Each
carries version="<year>" and (except 2014) an "Ucinnost" line naming the first
period it applies to — but a REVISED kv_dph_2025.xsd would still say
version="2025" and Ucinnost 1.1.2025, so it is indistinguishable from the copy
we hold. Nothing in the file changes when the file changes. The same trap as
the Czech `verzePis`, where a stale literal validates exactly as cleanly as a
current one; here it is the whole schema rather than one attribute.

So "our copy is current" is answerable only by comparing against what is
published, and only at the instant you compare. These digests turn that into
something a later run can check rather than a fact that was true once.

REFRESH PROCEDURE
  1. For each file above, fetch
     https://ekr.financnasprava.sk/Formulare/XSD/<filename>
     and compare the md5 with the line here.
  2. Check the status code, not the size: a miss returns 404 with a ~1 245-byte
     HTML error page, which parses as neither XSD nor nothing. Anything that
     tests presence by size installs an error page as a form.
  3. Probe for a NEWER vintage separately — kv_dph_2026.xsd and so on. A new
     vzor is a new file here, unlike the Czech side where the single file is
     overwritten in place. Absence of a newer file is a 404, present ones 200.
  4. If a digest moved: replace the file, update this line, and re-run the
     export tests. There is no changelog; diffing the two copies is the only
     way to see what changed.

LOWER BOUNDS. 2016, 2023 and 2025 date themselves through their Ucinnost
lines. kv_dph_2014.xsd carries NO Ucinnost, so its lower bound cannot come
from the file: 2014-01-01 in the version record is the statutory start of the
kontrolný výkaz obligation (§ 78a zákona č. 222/2004 Z. z.), and there is
nothing in the schema to check it against. Recorded here because that makes it
the one date in the module that no automated check can defend.
